#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:4
msgid "The C interface JSON file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:6
msgid "The ``gdextension_interface.json`` file is the \"source of truth\" for the C API that Godot uses to communicate with GDExtensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:9
msgid "You can use the Godot executable to dump the file by using the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:15
msgid "This file is intended to be used by GDExtension language bindings to generate code for using this API in whatever form makes the most sense for that language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:20
msgid "This is not to be confused with the ``extension_api.json``, which is also used by GDExtension language bindings, and contains information about the classes and methods that are exposed by Godot. The ``gdextension_interface.json`` is more low-level, and is used to interact with those higher-level classes and methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:25
msgid "For languages that can be extended via C, or provide tools for interacting with C code, it's also possible to use the Godot executable to dump a generated C header file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:34
msgid "The header file is compatible with earlier versions of the header file that were included with Godot 4.5 and earlier, which means it preserves some typos in names in order to ensure compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:38
msgid "The goal of this page is to explain the JSON format for the GDExtension language bindings that would like to do their own code generation from the JSON."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:42
msgid "Overall structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:44
msgid "The JSON file is broken up into 3 sections:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:46
msgid "The header, which includes some miscellaneous information at the top-level of the JSON file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:47
msgid "The ``types`` key, which defines all the types used in the GDExtension interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:48
msgid "The ``interface`` key, which defines all the function pointers that can be loaded via the ``GDExtensionInterfaceGetProcAddress`` function pointer, which is passed to all GDExtensions when they are loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:52
msgid "There is a complete `JSON schema <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/extension/gdextension_interface.schema.json>`__ included in Godot's source code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:55
msgid "Even though we may add new types and interface functions with each minor release of Godot, we strive to **never** change them in a backwards incompatible way, or remove them. Every interface function is labeled with the version of Godot it was introduced in (the ``since`` key), so you can always use the latest version of the file, and simply refrain from using anything in versions of Godot that are newer than the version you are targeting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:62
msgid "Header"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:64
msgid "The \"header\" is made up of 3 miscellaneous keys at the top-level of the file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:66
msgid "``_copyright``: The standard copyright and license text that Godot includes in all source code files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:68
msgid "``$schema``: Points to the JSON schema relative to this file. It can be useful to place the schema in the same directory, if you're viewing it with a code editor that understands JSON schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:71
msgid "``format_version``: An integer for the version of the file format (meaning the schema). Right now, there is only one format version (``1``). If we ever change the file format in an incompatible way, we will increment this number. This *doesn't* reflect the version of the data in the file (so it won't change between Godot versions), only its format. Hopefully, we'll never have to use it, but it allows code generators to error early if they encounter an unexpected value here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:79
msgid "Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:81
msgid "The ``types`` section is an array of types that will be used by other types, and the interface functions that will be in the last section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:84
msgid "The types should be evaluated in order. Later types may refer to earlier types, but earlier types will not refer to later types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:87
msgid "There is a small set of built-in types which aren't explicitly listed in the JSON:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:89
msgid "``void``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:90
msgid "``int8_t``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:91
msgid "``uint8_t``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:92
msgid "``int16_t``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:93
msgid "``uint16_t``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:94
msgid "``int32_t``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:95
msgid "``uint32_t``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:96
msgid "``int64_t``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:97
msgid "``uint64_t``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:98
msgid "``size_t`` (``uint32_t`` on 32-bit architectures, and ``uint64_t`` on 64-bit architectures)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:99
msgid "``char``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:100
msgid "``char16_t``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:101
msgid "``char32_t``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:102
msgid "``wchar_t``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:103
msgid "``float``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:104
msgid "``double``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:106
msgid "These correspond to their equivalent C types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:108
msgid "Additionally, types can include modifiers such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:110
msgid "``*`` (e.g. ``int8_t*``) to indicate a pointer to the type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:111
msgid "``const`` (e.g. ``const int8_t*``) to indicate a const type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:113
msgid "Each type defined in the JSON file falls into one of 5 \"kinds\":"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:115
msgid "``enum``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:116
msgid "``handle``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:117
msgid "``alias``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:118
msgid "``struct``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:119
msgid "``function``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:121
msgid "Regardless of the \"kind\", all types can have the following keys:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:123
msgid "``kind`` (required): The type's \"kind\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:124
msgid "``name`` (required): The name of the type, which could be used as a valid C identifier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:125
msgid "``description``: An array of strings documenting the type, where each string is a line of documentation (this format for ``description`` is used throughout the JSON file)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:127
msgid "``deprecated``: An object with its own keys for the Godot version the type was deprecated in (``since``), a message explaining the deprecation (``message``), and optionally a replacement to use instead (``replacement``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:132
msgid "Enums"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:134
msgid "Enums are 32-bit integers with a fixed set of possible values. In C, they could be represented as an ``enum``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:137
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:183
msgid "They have the following keys:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:139
msgid "``is_bitfield``: If true, this enum is a bitfield, where the enum values can be bitwise OR'd together. It is false by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:141
msgid "``values``: The array of fixed values for this enum, each with a ``name``, ``value``, and ``description``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:143
msgid "An enum should be represented as an ``int32_t``, unless ``is_bitfield`` is true, in which case a ``uint32_t`` should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:147
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:196
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:217
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:239
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:277
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:321
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:179
msgid "Handles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:181
msgid "Handles are pointers to opaque structs. In C, they could be represented as ``void *`` or ``struct{} *``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:185
msgid "``is_const``: If true, this handle type is to be treated as a \"const pointer\", meaning its internal data will not be changed. It is false by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:187
msgid "``is_uninitialized``: If true, this handle type is to be treated as pointing to uninitialized memory (which may be initialized using interface functions). It is false by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:189
msgid "``parent``: The optional name of another handle type, if this handle type is the const or uninitialized version of the parent type. This only makes sense if either ``is_const`` or ``is_uninitialized`` is true."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:192
msgid "Handles are the size of pointers on the given architecture (so, 64-bit on x86_64 and 32-bit on x86_32, for example)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:206
msgid "Aliases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:208
msgid "Aliases are alternative names for a type. In C, they could be represented as a ``typedef``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:210
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:233
msgid "They have only one additional key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:212
msgid "``type``: The type the alias is an alternative name for. It may include modifiers as described above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:214
msgid "These should be represented using the same C type as the type they refer to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:228
msgid "Structs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:230
msgid "Structs represent C ``struct``\\ s (aka a block of memory made up of the given members in order), and should follow all the same layout and alignment rules as C structs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:235
msgid "``members``: An array of objects which have a ``name``, ``type`` (which may include modifiers), and ``description``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:263
msgid "Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:265
msgid "Functions represent C function pointer types, with a list of arguments and a return type, and should follow the same size and alignment requirements as C function pointers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:268
msgid "They have the following members:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:270
msgid "``return_value``: An object which has a ``type`` (which may include modifiers) and ``description``. If the function has no return value, this will be omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:272
msgid "``arguments`` (required): An array of function arguments which each has a ``type`` (which may include modifiers), ``name``, and ``description``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:297
msgid "Interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:299
msgid "The ``interface`` section of the JSON file is the list of interface functions, which can be loaded by ``name`` using the ``GDExtensionInterfaceGetProcAddress`` function pointer, which is passed to all GDExtensions when they are loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:303
msgid "Interface functions have some of the same keys as types, including ``name`` (required), ``deprecated``, and ``description``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:306
msgid "And they also have ``return_value`` and ``arguments`` (required) that have the same format as the equivalent keys on function types (as described in the previous section)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:309
msgid "There are only a handful of unique keys:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:311
msgid "``since`` (required): The Godot version that introduced this interface function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:312
msgid "``see``: An array of strings describing external references with more information, for example, names of classes or functions in the Godot source code, or URLs pointing to documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/gdextension_interface_json_file.rst:314
msgid "``legacy_type_name``: The legacy name used for the function pointer type in the header generated by Godot, when the legacy name doesn't match the pattern used for these type names. This field only exists so that we can generate the header in a way that is backwards compatible with the header from Godot 4.5 or earlier, and it shouldn't be used unless you also need to maintain compatibility with the old header."
msgstr ""
